index fa1a2d5..3ee83de 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,18 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Tool input declared in a tool's `inputSchema` is now enforced by `ToolRegistry.execute` before the
+  executor runs. A call the schema rejects — a missing required property, a value of the wrong type —
+  comes back to the model as a readable tool result naming the property and the constraint that
+  failed, within the existing tool-round budget, instead of ending the turn with a generic error.
+  The message never echoes the offending value. Executors receive only input the schema already
+  accepts, so one that hand-validated its own input or defaulted missing fields can drop that code;
+  a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message stops seeing it.
+  Extra properties the schema does not declare pass through unchanged, and a schema that cannot
+  compile fails at `register` time rather than mid-conversation.
+
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17
 
 ### Changed
